odox (0.4.0) unstable; urgency=low

  * The three applications edit. A window opens reading and Ctrl+E turns
    editing on; a preference opens every document that way. In xodt a
    click on a paragraph opens it as a text box where it sits; Enter
    starts a new paragraph and Backspace at the start joins two. In xods
    typing on the picked cell replaces it, Enter or F2 opens it, and
    Delete clears it; a formula cell is kept and not edited. In xodp a
    shape is dragged, resized by a corner, and its text edited in place.
  * Save and Save as, undo and redo, and a question before changes are
    thrown away. Before a save the bytes are read back and compared with
    the document in the window, and a difference refuses the save.
  * What was not touched is written back as it was read, element for
    element. The tests mutate every paragraph of every corpus document
    and check that.
  * One preference, in odox/settings.toml under the configuration
    directory, written only when it is changed.
  * A proportional line height is a proportion of each run's own size, so
    a title whose size lives on its span no longer sits in a line the
    height of its paragraph's default.
  * The desktop entries, the package descriptions and the man pages say
    editor rather than viewer.

 -- David M. Anderson <david.anderson@excelano.com>  Mon, 21 Sep 2026 15:08:24 -0500

odox (0.3.0) unstable; urgency=low

  * xodp draws five more of what a slide is made of: draw:path outlines,
    connectors routed between the shapes they join, the labels a shape carries
    directly, and shapes placed by draw:transform, which are the turned
    decorations a template is recognised by and which were dropped entirely
    before this.
  * A frame offering its picture twice, as an SVG and then a PNG, now takes the
    first one that can be decoded rather than the first one listed.
  * Opening a document no longer aborts. A document names font families,
    registering them takes effect on the next frame, and the document was drawn
    in the frame that opened it. Reachable by dropping a document on the window
    or with Ctrl+O.
  * Groundwork for Windows and macOS, neither of which ships yet.

 -- David M. Anderson <david.anderson@excelano.com>  Mon, 14 Sep 2026 21:45:55 -0500

odox (0.2.1) unstable; urgency=low

  * The odox package depends on the three viewers rather than recommending
    them, so apt install odox installs the whole suite.

